P-HUBLEG.claim:
In game, untraced, before run 1, the harness drives the pick and the hub throws nothing. The steps:
- log_mark;
- New Game;
- hub_leg up to the options (warp 31100 0 2540, a blind calibrate_axes, walk_to east with strict=False and slides=True, interact, at most 3 tries);
- the choice offers exactly ["Dali (SC 2600)", "Stay here, kupo..."] with the cursor on 0;
- selecting "Stay here, kupo..." with the guarded Confirm leaves him in 31100 with control and no field change for 60 frames;
- exceptions_since(mark) holds no THROWS type with an EventEngine, EBin, StoryTrace or HarnessAgent frame;
- the title is restored.
It records the measured r, talk_r and approach point.

R5-REACH.claim:
The fork does not stop where stock goes on.
Every non-covered F5 run with a covered partner has a frozen stop class: DRIVE (the walker, the budget, the channel, the install; never evidence) or FORK-STOP at a point. The FORK-STOP points are:
- 'hub': the stamps landed, 31111 was never reached;
- 'segment@<place>': no wake, or a live soft-lock or re-asked choice in the segment;
- 'replay@<step>': a crossing entered another place, struck out REAL, or left him elsewhere;
- 'scene@<place>@<sc>': a live soft-lock in the replay or tour.
In sessions 3 and 4, 6/6 F0 replays completed with 0 breaks, every S segment and 6/6 F4 segments at SC 2600 were ok, and session 4's S walks were identical, so a fork-caused stop repeats on the same walk.

R5-STAMP.claim:
The hub's rows are the frozen seed. Read from each F5 run's RAW trace (read_run5 keeps split[0]; never r['pre'], which is a field list). Every row in 31100 is joined by ScriptIndex.join against the snapshotted hub .eb (a store, verified offline at +23/+31/+39; ip+1 fails). In every F5 run that reached 31111:
(1) the rows in 31100 are only e0 t0 stores to the prologue targets plus exactly three stamps in e2 t3, in order: UInt16[0] 2540->2600 at +23, UInt16[208] 0->0 at +31, UInt16[297] 0->1 at +39;
(2) every row in 31100 has src eb (no cs, no harness row; session 4 had none) and don 31100;
(3) the next placed row after the last hub row is in 31111;
(4) the width clause: each stamp row's changed neighbour bytes (other than its start) have an empty storytrace.outside_target(stock_layout(covered S digests), start, byte). On New Game state every neighbour is unchanged, so this clause is vacuous on real data; it guards the round-4 defect class.
In runs that never reached 31111, the 31100 rows must still satisfy (1)-(2) up to where they stop, and (3) wherever a placed row follows the last hub row (AMENDED at the fix, before any deploy: a pick that led elsewhere -- the stamps, then a first member row in 31104 -- never reaches 31111, and only (3) can see it; the registered mutant needs it).

R5-MIRROR.claim:
S vs F5 over each whole run from its start field (the segment, the paired tour window, Garnet's scene): FORK ONLY, STOCK ONLY, ACROSS SEAM and SEAM ONLY are empty, and there is no neighbour-byte clobber among member keys. It is not vacuous, read on the stock side:
- at least 200 keys appear in every covered S run (session 4: 286);
- at least 110 are first written in every S tour, from donors including {350, 351, 354, 355, 356, 450} (session 4: 167);
- at least 40 are first written at or after each S run's first row in 450, from donors including {350, 354, 356, 450} (session 4: 72).

R5-ADVANCE.claim:
The story advances to 2610 in a member, at the partner's step. In every covered F5 run:
- its first placed row at SC >= 2610 is 354 e13 t1 +1152 UInt16[0]:=2610 in member(354) (31106, don 354);
- that key is MATCHED;
- the advance falls on the same entered-walk step as its partner's (session 4: step 24, [350, 1, 354]).
F5 coverage does not require the advance.
